# Andes CSR coverage matrix

Authoritative map of every CSR in `AndeStar_V5_SPA_UM164_V1.7` against the hybrid
handoff, for the supported envelope: **bare-metal, single-hart, M-mode or M+U-mode,
trap-free ROI**. This is the "nothing missed" artifact -- the spec's Chapter 5
summary tables yield 232 CSR rows, and every one has a disposition below.

Generated from the committed snapshot `tests/andes_csr/csr_inventory.csv`
(re-extract with `scripts/extract_csr_inventory.py <spec.pdf>`) classified by
`scripts/classify_csr_coverage.py` (the offline mirror of the ABI transport set).
The guard test `tests/andes_csr/test_csr_coverage_complete.*` fails CI if the spec
inventory, this matrix, and `include/hybrid/state_abi.h` ever drift apart.

## Dispositions

| disposition | meaning | tested by |
|-------------|---------|-----------|
| **carried today** | already in `hybrid_state_v1`; restored + drained + `--verify` | per-section round-trip fixture |
| **ADD** | writable M-mode plain state; expansion target (this ROADMAP) | per-section round-trip fixture |
| **ADD (trigger\*)** | debug-trigger CSR; transported with care (shares the Debug Module) | trigger fixture (guarded) |
| **ADD (M+U)** | U-mode Andes control; transported, exercised only in M+U | deferred (premium is M-only) |
| **excl: read-only config** | machine-info / config register; each engine derives it from its own config -- no state to exchange | constant-agreement check |
| **excl: RV32-only** | RV32 high-half shadow; irrelevant on RV64 | n/a |
| **excl: side-effecting** | read or write triggers an action (push to stack, issue cache op, swap scratch) -- not architectural state | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: W1C/HW-driven** | write-1-clear status owned by hardware (like `mip`) | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: indirect-access** | `miselect`/`mireg` access mechanism, not a direct register | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: N-ext trap** | U-mode N-extension trap state; trap-free ROI + typically unimplemented | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: debug-internal** | Debug-mode CSR the handoff mechanism itself drives | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: mode unsupported** | S-mode or Hypervisor -- outside the M / M+U product envelope | exclusion assertion |
| **excl: trap-cause** | detailed trap-cause latch, live only after a trap | exclusion assertion |

\* Triggers share the Debug Module the handoff uses; transporting them is gated
and verified separately (see ROADMAP feature F-TRIG).

